# FREE-TIER DEPLOYMENT OVERRIDES (2026-11-19) — READ BEFORE EDITING.
# This file is COMMITTED (force-added; .env.* is gitignored) because it is
# deployment config, not secrets: it carries no keys, only feature flags.
# Why it exists: the gh token that pushes this fork has no `workflow` scope,
# so the workflow files' env flags (.github/workflows/*.yaml) cannot be
# edited from here. config.py loads .env.local with override=True at import
# (constants.py:185), so these values win over the workflow's `true`
# settings in Actions.
# What it disables, and why (all four fail on a $0 / no-key account and turn
# every run red via the alert policy, even though the forecast publishes):
#   NATIVE_SEARCH_ENABLED=false — the web-search plugin 402s on a $0
#     account, and free models don't support native web search (404).
#   GEMINI_SEARCH_ENABLED=false — no GOOGLE_API_KEY is configured.
#   GAP_FILL_ENABLED=false — the v1 analyzer runs but its resolvers need
#     the paid web plugin, so every gap 404s.
#   GAP_FILL_V2_ENABLED=false — its driver is a paid model (402).
# To re-enable (e.g. when donated credits arrive): delete this file — the
# workflow flags are `true` — and set the workflow flags back to `true` if
# they were ever flipped to `false` in the meantime.
# Local tests are unaffected: all four flags default to false in code, so
# these values are identical to the defaults; tests that need a feature set
# the flag via monkeypatch after import, which wins over this file.
NATIVE_SEARCH_ENABLED=false
GEMINI_SEARCH_ENABLED=false
GAP_FILL_ENABLED=false
GAP_FILL_V2_ENABLED=false
